  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Process Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Process Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Process and STAT",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Process== = running program with a **PID** and **PPID** (parent)",
                "Every process has a parent; ==PID 1== (init/systemd) is the ancestor"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "STAT",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "R",
                  "running"
                ],
                [
                  "S",
                  "sleeping"
                ],
                [
                  "D",
                  "I/O wait, ==cannot be killed=="
                ],
                [
                  "T",
                  "stopped"
                ],
                [
                  "Z",
                  "==zombie==: exited, parent has not called wait"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Control layers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Signal",
                    "sub": "kernel's message",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Job",
                    "sub": "shell handle",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Service",
                    "sub": "systemd: logs, restart",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Foreground jobs own the terminal",
                "Background jobs die on hangup unless `nohup` or `disown`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Zombie vs orphan?** Zombie: exited, parent never called wait. Orphan: parent died, child still runs",
                "**Why can't `kill -9` remove a zombie?** Already dead; only the parent's wait reaps it",
                "**PID 1 and orphans?** It adopts them and reaps them on exit"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Inspecting Processes with ps and top",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Inspecting Processes with ps and top",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ps vs top",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ps` = ==one-time snapshot==, use it in scripts",
                "`top` = ==live refresh==, use it to watch load",
                "`ps aux` (BSD): USER PID %CPU %MEM VSZ RSS STAT COMMAND",
                "`ps -ef` (POSIX): adds ==PPID== and the full command line"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Filtering",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ps -p PID` shows one process",
                "`pgrep -a nginx` lists PID and command by name",
                "`ps aux | grep [n]ginx`: the ==[n]== trick stops grep matching itself"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. top keys and load",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Key",
                "Action"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`P`",
                  "sort by CPU"
                ],
                [
                  "`M`",
                  "sort by memory"
                ],
                [
                  "`1`",
                  "per-core CPU"
                ],
                [
                  "`k`",
                  "kill a PID"
                ],
                [
                  "`q`",
                  "quit"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Load average = ==1, 5, 15 min== values",
                "Load above the **core count** = saturated"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**VSZ vs RSS?** VSZ is virtual size; ==RSS== is real RAM in use",
                "**Top memory user?** `ps aux --sort=-%mem | head`, or `M` in top",
                "**Load average?** Runnable and waiting tasks, averaged over 1/5/15 min"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Jobs: Foreground and Background",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Jobs: Foreground and Background",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Controlling Jobs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Action",
                "Keys / command",
                "Signal"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Start in background",
                  "`cmd &`",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Suspend foreground",
                  "==Ctrl+Z==",
                  "SIGTSTP"
                ],
                [
                  "Interrupt foreground",
                  "==Ctrl+C==",
                  "SIGINT"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`jobs` lists this shell's jobs as ==[1]+==",
                "`fg %1` brings job 1 to the foreground",
                "`bg %1` resumes a stopped job in the background"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Run long cmd",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ctrl+Z",
                    "sub": "stopped",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bg",
                    "sub": "keeps running",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fg",
                    "sub": "back on terminal",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Surviving Hangup",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Closing the terminal sends ==SIGHUP==, which kills background jobs",
                "`nohup cmd &` ignores HUP; output goes to ==nohup.out==",
                "`disown -h %n` protects a job that is already running"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "nohup ./backup.sh &   # job %1",
                "sleep 600 &           # job %2",
                "disown -h %2          # already running"
              ],
              "note": "disown -h takes the job number"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Only nohup writes nohup.out",
              "text": "`disown -h` just stops SIGHUP. Output still goes to the closed terminal."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Foreground to background?** Ctrl+Z, then `bg`",
                "**Why do jobs die on SSH close?** SIGHUP. Use `nohup` or `disown -h`",
                "**jobs vs ps?** `jobs` shows this shell's jobs; `ps` shows system processes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Signals, kill and Exit Codes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Signals, kill and Exit Codes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Signals and kill",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`kill PID` sends ==SIGTERM (15)==: catchable, so the process cleans up and exits",
                "`kill -9 PID` sends ==SIGKILL==: {red:cannot be caught or ignored, no cleanup}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Num",
                "Signal",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1",
                  "HUP",
                  "reload config / hangup"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "INT",
                  "Ctrl+C"
                ],
                [
                  "9",
                  "KILL",
                  "uncatchable"
                ],
                [
                  "15",
                  "TERM",
                  "default, catchable"
                ],
                [
                  "18",
                  "CONT",
                  "resume"
                ],
                [
                  "19",
                  "STOP",
                  "pause, uncatchable"
                ],
                [
                  "20",
                  "TSTP",
                  "Ctrl+Z"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Kill by name",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`killall name`: by process name",
                "`pkill -f pattern`: by full command line",
                "Preview first with `pgrep -a pattern`: matches can hit {red:unrelated} processes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Exit codes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "0",
                  "success"
                ],
                [
                  "nonzero",
                  "failure"
                ],
                [
                  "126",
                  "not executable"
                ],
                [
                  "127",
                  "command not found"
                ],
                [
                  "128+N",
                  "killed by signal N"
                ],
                [
                  "137 / 143",
                  "SIGKILL / SIGTERM"
                ],
                [
                  "`echo $?`",
                  "last command's code"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why TERM before KILL?** TERM lets the process clean up; KILL skips cleanup",
                "**What does 137 mean?** 128+9: killed by ==SIGKILL==, often OOM or a stop timeout",
                "**Did the last command succeed?** `echo $?`, and 0 means yes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "systemd Services and journalctl",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "systemd Services and journalctl",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Unit Files",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==PID 1== starts and supervises every **service**",
                "Unit file: `/etc/systemd/system/app.service`",
                "`[Unit]` ordering, `[Service]` how to run, `[Install]` boot target"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ini",
              "lines": [
                "[Unit]",
                "After=network.target",
                "[Service]",
                "ExecStart=/usr/bin/app",
                "User=app",
                "Restart=on-failure",
                "[Install]",
                "WantedBy=multi-user.target"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lifecycle",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`start` / `stop`",
                  "now only, gone after reboot"
                ],
                [
                  "`enable` / `disable`",
                  "boot only, not started now"
                ],
                [
                  "`enable --now`",
                  "enable + start"
                ],
                [
                  "`restart`",
                  "stop, then start a new process"
                ],
                [
                  "`reload`",
                  "re-read config, same process"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Edited a unit? Run ==systemctl daemon-reload==",
                "`systemctl status app` shows state; `systemctl --failed` lists failures"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Logs with journalctl",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Shows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`-u app`",
                  "one service's logs"
                ],
                [
                  "`-f`",
                  "follow live"
                ],
                [
                  "`-n 100`",
                  "last 100 lines"
                ],
                [
                  "`--since '1 hour ago'`",
                  "recent window"
                ],
                [
                  "`-p err`",
                  "errors and worse"
                ],
                [
                  "`-b`",
                  "current boot only"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Crash loop: `systemctl status app`, then `journalctl -u app -b -p err`"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "start is not enable",
              "text": "`start` does not survive a reboot, and `enable` does not start now. Use ==enable --now== for both."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
